@@ -32,6 +32,50 @@ absolute canonical path before importing `@gpuix/native`. Application bindings
 must load that same file. Loading a second addon creates separate native state.
 This extension API does not add multi-window support.
 
+### Admitting extension tags in Solid
+
+After the application installs its native factories, register their names in
+the framework-neutral host schema before mounting Solid:
+
+```tsx
+import { registerCustomElementType } from '@gpuix/native/host'
+import type { HostProps } from '@gpuix/native/host'
+import type { SolidHostProps } from '@gpuix/solid/jsx-runtime'
+
+registerCustomElementType('acme-panel')
+
+declare module '@gpuix/solid/jsx-runtime' {
+  namespace JSX {
+    interface IntrinsicElements {
+      'acme-panel': SolidHostProps<HostProps & { label: string }>
+    }
+  }
+}
+// Inside a normal createRoot(renderer).render callback:
+// <acme-panel label={reactiveLabel()} onClick={onClick} />
+```
+
+`registerCustomElementType(name)` accepts lowercase ASCII hyphen-separated
+names (for example `acme-panel`), rejects built-in overrides including
+`virtual-list`, and returns a branded `CustomElementType` assignable to
+`ElementType`. Repeating registration is idempotent across module reloads.
+`isHostElementType(name)` recognizes built-ins plus registered custom names;
+`isCustomElementType(name)` recognizes only the registered names. These exports
+are shared by adapters and do not import the addon. Registration never creates
+a native registry/instance, installs a factory, or seals native startup. The
+schema is process-local and additive; there is no runtime unregister operation.
+
+Solid rejects unregistered names rather than rendering a fallback. On macOS,
+`GpuixRenderer.hasCustomElementType(name)` inspects that initialized window's
+existing native factory registry without creating an instance. It rejects
+uninitialized or closed windows. Solid checks this capability before mounting
+registered custom elements and throws a clear missing-factory error instead of
+letting native render an empty element. Other backends without the optional
+query still require explicit JS registration but cannot prove native availability.
+Initialize the renderer before mounting; use the same installed addon for both
+the host and framework. Custom props, events and instance lifetimes then use the
+normal Solid mutation path, including reactive updates and unmount/remount.
+
 ## Multiple native windows on macOS
 
 Create one `GpuixRenderer` per window and call `init` on each. They share one
